# Task Workflow

## Before starting

1. Read `docs/project/05-current-state.md` and confirm the next TASK.
2. Read the **entire** `docs/tasks/TASK-NNN-*.md` file.
3. Keep Scope / Out of Scope / Acceptance Criteria in mind.
4. **Search** existing code for similar implementations or patterns before adding anything new; avoid duplication.

## During implementation

- Work on **one TASK at a time**.
- Search existing implementation one more time before adding a new file, function, or pattern.
- **Every CLI command should support `--dry-run` (or equivalent) where possible** so it can show the plan without file, Git, or remote mutations.
- Do not touch the next TASK file before the current TASK finishes.

## Lifecycle commands

| Stage    | Command                                                         |
| -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Start    | `vibeops task start TASK-NNN`                                   |
| Work     | `vibeops task prompt TASK-NNN --agent builder` → paste into Cursor |
| Check    | `vibeops task check TASK-NNN`                                   |
| Complete | `vibeops task done TASK-NNN` (no automatic merge)               |
| Rollback | `vibeops task rollback TASK-NNN` (guidance by default; destructive work requires `--confirm`) |

## Completion criteria

- All Acceptance Criteria pass.
- **Result** and **Test Result** in the TASK file are not empty.
- `docs/project/05-current-state.md` and `docs/logs/YYYY-MM-DD.md` are updated.

The TASK is not complete until all three are reflected.
